  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASPIRE &#x2013; Addressing Social Protection in Isolated and Rural areas, with Early childhood nutrition, livelihoods, and climate change activities.The ASPIRE programme is a multi-sectoral approach to tackle the root causes of malnutrition, including agriculture, WASH, and social protection. The pilot phase of the project included a climate vulnerability capacity analysis (CVCA) in the targeted communities to assess their vulnerability to climate change to inform the development of a capacity adaptation plan, and these plans will now be enacted in a phased manner. It also includes support for womens leadership in CSLAs and income generation activities.</narrative>
  </description>
